(2,'🟢',"Container versus virtual machine, for an ML engineer. Explain namespaces (pid, net, mnt), cgroups (cpu, memory), a shared host kernel, startup time and isolation trade-offs, why a container cannot ship its own kernel or GPU driver, and what that means for a model that needs a specific CUDA driver. Say when a VM or a micro-VM is the better boundary (untrusted code, multi-tenant notebooks).",GEN),
(2,'🟡',"Container killed with exit code 137 or a DataLoader crash 'bus error, shared memory'. Explain what exit 137 means (SIGKILL, often the OOM killer), the difference between --memory limits and host memory, how Python and PyTorch memory behave under a cgroup limit, why DataLoader workers need /dev/shm (default 64 MB in Docker; fix with --shm-size or --ipc=host), and how to confirm OOM (docker inspect OOMKilled, dmesg). Show the run flags and a Python script that reads cgroup memory limits from /sys/fs/cgroup if present.",GEN),
