(2,'🟡',"Multi-architecture images and the Apple Silicon problem. A developer builds on an M-series Mac and the image fails on the amd64 GPU server with 'exec format error', or wheels are missing for arm64. Explain architectures (amd64, arm64), docker buildx build --platform, QEMU emulation speed, manifest lists, building in CI on native runners, and checking an image's architecture. Show buildx commands; run docker buildx version and docker buildx build --help here and say that real builds were not executed.",BK),
(2,'🟡',"A long training job in a container on spot or pre-emptible instances. Explain how to write checkpoints to a mounted volume or object store, resume logic in the entrypoint, handling SIGTERM to save a last checkpoint within the stop grace period (docker stop -t), idempotent output paths, logging to stdout, and why exit codes matter for orchestrators. Show a Python training-loop skeleton with a SIGTERM handler that you actually run and kill with a signal, and a docker run command (not executed).",JOB),
(2,'🟡',"Installing Python dependencies in an image: pip, uv, conda or micromamba. Compare speed, lockfiles, binary compatibility, and size; pip --no-cache-dir versus a BuildKit cache mount; installing torch from the CPU or CUDA wheel index with --index-url; the venv-in-image pattern for multi-stage copying; and why you should not run pip as root without a venv in some setups. Say when conda is justified in Docker (non-Python native stacks). Show two Dockerfile variants and compare the size by reasoning, not by claimed numbers.",BK),
(2,'🟡',"Debugging a container that will not start or keeps restarting. Walk through docker ps -a, docker logs, docker inspect (ExitCode, OOMKilled, State.Error), docker run --entrypoint sh -it to get a shell, docker exec, docker events, and causes such as 'exec format error', a script with CRLF line endings ('no such file or directory' on the shebang), a missing executable bit, wrong WORKDIR, a missing shared library, and a port conflict. Give a triage order and a table of symptom to cause. Commands not executed; parse a sample inspect JSON with python.",GEN),
